version.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The requested environment capability is the blogwatcher binary, which is proportionate to the skill's stated purpose; no broad filesystem indexing, credential use, or privileged execution is requested by the skill artifact.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The install metadata and manual command use go install with github.com/Hyaxia/blogwatcher/cmd/blogwatcher@latest, which is disclosed and coherent for a Go CLI but is mutable rather than pinned to a reviewed release.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime instructions are simple usage examples for the CLI and do not attempt to override agent behavior, alter safety constraints, access unrelated data, or hide secondary actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill does not define background services, scheduled tasks, persistent hooks, memory writes, privilege escalation, or tool replacement behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to monitor blogs and RSS/Atom feeds, and the documented commands are limited to installing and using the blogwatcher CLI for feed management and article status.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, consider pinning blogwatcher to a specific reviewed version instead of @latest, and install it only in an environment where the CLI does not inherit unnecessary secrets or sensitive filesystem access.","findings":"[T08] expected: Installing a third-party Go CLI is expected for this skill, but the @latest selector means future upstream changes determine what gets installed; this is a supply-chain caution rather than evidence of hidden or malicious behavior in the skill artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1